  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 213 PM MDT Tue Oct 20 2026\n\nA large upper trough will continue spinning away off the coast of \nCalifornia. Meanwhile an upper high is to our southeast. This will \nfocus moisture and chances for storms over AZ and our western \nportions of the CWA Wednesday. A Marginal Risk is out tomorrow \nhighlighting the Continental Divide and west for strong storms that \ncould produce severe hail and severe wind gusts. The aforementioned \ntrough lifts out over the Lower CO Basin Thursday but this will \nspell a very active couple days for the area with potential for \nflooding, and strong storms that could produce hail and severe wind \ngusts. Abnormally moist conditions on the way Thursday where PWs \nwill reach up to 1.1\" to 1.2\" which is record breaking, or at least \nnear record breaking, which will add to the flooding threat.\n\nBehind the main aforementioned trough, another low cuts off and \ngives us a little more energy for Saturdays storms. Continued rain \nand thunderstorm chances Saturday where severe thunderstorms are \npossible once again, as well as flooding. By the end of the weekend, \nthis trough finally gets sucked into the main flow allowing some \ndrier and clearing conditions from west to east. Another strong cold \nfront possible Monday into Tuesday with windy conditions.",
